  "notes": "{蹴躓|けつまず}く describes physically tripping or figuratively encountering setbacks.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n\nWRITING:\nOften written in hiragana as けつまずく or with partial kanji as {躓|つまず}く. The kanji {蹴|け} (kick) and {躓|つまず}く (stumble) combine to form the full word.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {石|いし}に{蹴躓|けつまず}く: to trip on a stone\n- {段差|だんさ}に{蹴躓|けつまず}く: to trip on a step\n- {計画|けいかく}が{蹴躓|けつまず}く: the plan stumbles\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {躓|つまず}く: variant form (same meaning)",
